// Edge case: prelude, host, and `extern` names are bindings in an outermost
// scope, so a top-level declaration may take one. The default policy is
// warn-and-allow: the declaration wins, the whole displaced subtree goes with
// it -- `list.each` below is a projection on the user's record, not the prelude
// builtin it would otherwise have been -- and the run reports that it happened.
def list = #{each = 7};

list.each

//@ expect-diagnostic: prelude or host name
//@ expect-last-value: 7
